  "2026-07-26T19:39:00.227Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: all-status searches for GH-752, unreadable list completeness, decoder drift, and storage integrity found shipped pm-cxyv/pm-iqgj/pm-hybj plus context owner pm-4k6b, but no item representing the distinct successful-partial-result contract reported in GitHub #752. Created open and intentionally unclaimed during the active SDK delivery tranche."
  "2026-07-27T07:35:32.026Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-07-27: selected after live all-status review of 2,129 items (1,807 closed, 309 open, 13 canceled; zero pre-existing in-progress), full canonical metadata/closed-lineage review, and GitHub/security/dependency inventory. This item is actively implemented in one cohesive public SDK/CLI integrity PR; unrelated backlog and container epics remain open and unclaimed."
  "2026-07-27T08:17:33.246Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: every list envelope now carries a source-corpus completeness certificate (complete, partial, or unchecked) with unreadable item/directory counts; --strict-read and SDK strictRead fail closed on partial scans and bypass index-only certainty. CLI contracts, MCP schemas, public SDK snapshots, docs, and complete/partial/index regressions are aligned. Full sandboxed coverage passed 377 files and 6,452 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-07-27T08:41:47.072Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: full release gate passed docs/skills, static quality, package boundary, token budgets, SDK snapshot/import costs, transport floor, 6452-test coverage at 100/100/100/100, version sync, secret scan, packed npm smoke, and 88-command package-first dogfood. Hosted analysis correctly deferred because the exact local SHA is not pushed yet. Fresh unrelated installed consumer resolved its own package binary and verified strict-read completeness=complete through direct, npx, and bunx execution."
